WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.306
Performance is trainable capability.

00:00:02.306 --> 00:00:09.095
People improve when they practice the right things, receive useful feedback, and correct errors over time.

00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:12.169
Experience alone does not guarantee improvement.

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:20.944
Someone can repeat the same pattern for years without getting better if the work never exposes weak points or gives them a way to adjust.

00:00:20.944 --> 00:00:24.915
Deliberate practice focuses on specific components of a skill.

00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:31.255
Instead of vaguely trying to get better at communication, a person might practice clearer handoffs.

00:00:31.255 --> 00:00:39.902
Instead of broadly trying to become a better analyst, they might practice evidence evaluation, assumption checking, or concise writing.

00:00:39.902 --> 00:00:44.897
Breaking skills into components makes improvement more visible and manageable.

00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:46.755
Feedback loops are essential.

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:53.096
Good feedback compares intention with outcome and arrives soon enough to influence future behavior.

00:00:53.096 --> 00:00:59.564
It can come from peers, mentors, metrics, simulation, rehearsal, review sessions, or self-reflection.

00:00:59.564 --> 00:01:02.318
The goal is not criticism for its own sake.

00:01:02.318 --> 00:01:07.058
The goal is correction that helps future performance become more reliable.

00:01:07.058 --> 00:01:10.196
Challenge should be balanced with recoverability.

00:01:10.196 --> 00:01:13.655
Practice that is too easy does not stretch capability.

00:01:13.655 --> 00:01:18.330
Practice that is too overwhelming can create confusion or discouragement.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:25.632
Simulation and rehearsal are useful because they let people prepare for difficult work before the stakes are high.

00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:31.012
Improvement is built through repetition with correction, not through busyness alone.

00:01:31.012 --> 00:01:34.983
Deliberate practice also requires selecting the right measure.

00:01:34.983 --> 00:01:39.530
Hours spent are easy to count, but they do not always show improvement.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:49.522
Better measures focus on error rate, clarity, speed with quality, decision accuracy, handoff quality, or the ability to perform under realistic constraints.

00:01:49.522 --> 00:01:53.300
The measure should reflect the skill that actually matters.
